# Therefore K2Cr2O7 behaves as oxidising agent only in acidic medium because in basic medium it converts into chromate not dichromate.
*   **Dichromate Structure:** Two tetrahedra share one corner ($Cr-O-Cr$ link). The $Cr-O-Cr$ bond angle is slightly larger than $109^\circ$ (=126^\circ)due to repulsion between the large chromate groups.
