## **IV. Comparative Summary: Lanthanoids vs. Actinoids**

| Feature | Lanthanoids (4f) | Actinoids (5f) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Max Oxidation State** | +4 | +7 (due to small energy gaps) |
| **Contraction** | Lanthanoid Contraction | More pronounced Actinoid Contraction |
| **Complex Formation** | Less tendency | Greater tendency |
| **Radioactivity** | Only Promethium (Pm, Z=61) | All are radioactive |
| **Energy Gap** | Larger gap (4f-5d) | Very small gap (5f-6d-7s) |

